{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROOT CAUSE CORRECTED — my first read of this ticket was WRONG and is retracted here.\n\nI initially read `fetch-secrets.sh:153-157` (\"All-blank => {\"tokens\": []} ... fails-closed until\nan operator populates >=1 PAT\") and concluded this was `environment-or-config`: an unpopulated\nSSM slot, no code defect, operator action only. Evidence says otherwise. The SSM parameters ARE\npopulated — all three, and they predate the crash:\n\n  /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-copilot  SecureString  2026-08-25T16:42:56Z\n  /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-codex    SecureString  2026-08-25T16:42:57Z\n  /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-claude   SecureString  2026-08-25T16:42:58Z\n\n(listed via get-parameters-by-path WITHOUT decryption; no values read or printed)\n\nTHE ACTUAL MECHANISM — a time skew, not a missing secret\nAn on-box measurement at 16:44:59Z, two minutes AFTER the PATs landed in SSM, printed\n`token_records= 0 []` — the on-disk mcp-static-tokens.json was still `{\"tokens\": []}`. A manual\n`fetch-secrets.sh` run at 16:45:45Z then printed `token_records= 3 ['copilot','codex','claude']`.\nPopulating an SSM SecureString advances no git ref, and nothing regenerates the on-disk file on\nits own. So: PATs land 16:42Z -> file stays empty -> an unrelated src/rebar change on main\ntriggers the mcp blue-green path -> the new container bind-mounts the STALE empty file -> fails\nclosed at `_mcp_auth.py:725`.\n\nThe error string is itself the discriminator. \"defines no tokens\" is the empty-ARRAY branch\n(line 725). Had the records been present but the env vars missing, the error would have been\nline 766 (\"'token_env' names env var ... unset or empty\"). It was not — so the file was empty,\nnot the environment.\n\nWhy the LIVE container works while new ones failed: `compose-mcp-1` was force-recreated at\n16:55Z, ten minutes AFTER the manual fetch-secrets run rewrote the file. Same path, same mount —\nthe containers differ only in WHEN they started. Ruled out: a different mount path\n(autodeploy.sh:365 mounts the same $COMPOSE_DIR file) and missing env (autodeploy.sh:352 passes\nthe same --env-file). Both were candidate explanations and both are refuted by the code.\n\nTWO LANDABLE REPO DEFECTS (so this is a code fix, not just an operator action)\n\nDefect A — the mcp blue-green path never refreshes SSM-sourced secrets.\n`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:621-700` does git checkout -> rsync -> build -> mcp_run_new and\ncalls fetch-secrets.sh ZERO times, yet it consumes two rsync-EXCLUDED, SSM-materialized\nartifacts: `.env` (autodeploy.sh:352) and `mcp-static-tokens.json` (autodeploy.sh:365). The\nreview-bot path already does exactly the right thing at autodeploy.sh:579, with a comment at\n:574-578 explaining why it is required (\"so new/rotated keys reach the container without a manual\nboot ... .env is rsync-EXCLUDED + SSM-sourced, so it is otherwise never regenerated on deploy\").\nThe mcp path was never given the same treatment. fetch-secrets is invoked only under the guard at\nautodeploy.sh:506, keyed on SECRETS_PATHS changing (autodeploy.sh:147) — and autodeploy.sh:144-146\nstates the gap outright: \"A pure SSM VALUE rotation with no git change does not advance main, so\nautodeploy no-ops on it.\"\n\nDefect B — the live working config is not reproducible from git and is self-destructing.\n`REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL` exists ONLY as a line an operator hand-appended to\n/opt/rebar/infra/compose/.env at 16:55Z. It is absent from the mcp `environment:` block and from\nmcp_run_new's -e list. fetch-secrets.sh regenerates .env WHOLESALE (mktemp + mv -f) and its\nheredoc does not emit that key — so the next fetch-secrets run DELETES the operator's fix and\nreverts the box to the 16:5xZ failure. Note the trap: fixing Defect A alone would TRIGGER Defect\nB, because A's whole point is to run fetch-secrets on every mcp deploy. They must land together.\n\nCorrection to the ticket's Summary: the compose file at docker-compose.yml:349-352 does carry a\n`${REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL:-https://...}` default with a comment citing bug\nhaughty-leisured-puffer. That default only applies to compose's own `environment:` interpolation;\nmcp_run_new builds its own -e list and does not inherit it, which is why the blue-green container\nstill lacked the value.\n\nSTILL UNDETERMINED (read-only limit): the alarm is STILL in ALARM and re-alarmed at 2026-08-26\n01:13Z, long after both known causes were satisfied on disk. deploy_errors datapoints continue\n(00:28Z, 00:43Z, 01:15Z, 01:30Z). Both known causes appear resolved on disk, so a THIRD failure\nmay be active. Confirming it needs `journalctl -u rebar-autodeploy` on the box, which requires\nan SSM send-command — a mutation, so out of scope without approval. Flagging rather than guessing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787712505791520001,"uuid":"26cffe32-a65b-4879-b1a7-641380b8fc1a"}